    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7168" root="حجر" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاجُورٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِجْرٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاجِرٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <i>A
refuge; a means of protection</i> or <i>defence:</i> analogous with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَاثُورٌ</span>, which signifies “a place of
perdition:” whence,
“<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَالَ قَائِلُهُمْ إِنَّى بِحَاجُورِ</span><br />
”
<i>And their sayer said, Verily I lay hold on that
which will protect me</i> from thee <i>and repel thee</i>
from me; <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَمَسِّكٌ</span> being understood. (TA.)

